  "captureVisualGuidesCardTitle": "Visual guides",
  "captureVisualGuidesAutoHeading": "Auto capture flow",
  "captureVisualGuidesOcrHeading": "Region OCR",
  "captureVisualGuidesPopupRefineHint": "Tip: In the capture popup, drag-select part of the source text to translate just that phrase—you can refine focus more than once without closing the popup.",
  "captureAutoFlowSelectLabel": "Select",
  "captureAutoFlowPauseLabel": "Pause",
  "captureAutoFlowPopupLabel": "Lookup",
  "captureAutoFlowCaption": "Typical flow when auto capture is on (other apps only).",
  "captureAutoVisualGuideLink": "Step-by-step guide with pictures…",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureTitle": "How auto capture works",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureIntro": "With Auto capture enabled, Formycareer watches for mouse-based text selection in other programs—not when you interact inside Formycareer itself.\n\nThe pictures below outline what happens.",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep1Title": "1. Select text elsewhere",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep1Body": "In a browser, PDF, or editor: drag across the words you want, or double-click a single word so it highlights.",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep2Title": "2. Release and wait briefly",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep2Body": "Let the highlight settle. A very short pause helps the app detect a stable selection.",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep3Title": "3. Popup opens",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep3Body": "The capture popup appears with the passage so you can translate, save, or review. Drag-select any substring in the source area to translate only that phrase.",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep4Title": "4. Pick another span in the source",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureStep4Body": "Whenever you want a different phrase, drag-select another span in the source area—the translation updates to match only that selection, and you can repeat this as many times as you like without closing the popup.",
  "captureDlgAutoCaptureSchemeCaption": "Schematic (not actual UI)",
  "captureOcrFlowHotkeyLabel": "Shortcut",
  "captureOcrFlowRegionLabel": "Region",
  "captureOcrFlowResultLabel": "OCR text",
  "captureOcrFlowCaption": "On-demand capture: Ctrl+Shift+X, then drag a rectangle over the text you want read.",
  "captureOcrVisualGuideLink": "OCR step-by-step with pictures…",
  "captureDlgOcrGuideTitle": "How region OCR works",
  "captureDlgOcrGuideIntro": "Region OCR reads text from a screen area you choose. It always runs when you trigger it—not tied to Auto capture.\n\nThe pictures below outline the flow.",
  "captureDlgOcrStep1Title": "1. Start region capture",
  "captureDlgOcrStep1Body": "Press Ctrl+Shift+X from another app, or use the in-app shortcut while this window is focused.",
  "captureDlgOcrStep2Title": "2. Drag a rectangle",
  "captureDlgOcrStep2Body": "The screen dims. Drag a box around the words or image text you want; adjust until the area looks right.",
  "captureDlgOcrStep3Title": "3. Confirm and review",
  "captureDlgOcrStep3Body": "Confirm the selection. Recognized text opens in the capture popup so you can translate or save it.",
  "captureDlgOcrStep4Title": "4. Pick another span in the source",
  "captureDlgOcrStep4Body": "Whenever you want a different phrase, drag-select another span in the source area—the translation updates to match only that selection, and you can repeat this as many times as you like without closing the popup.",
  "captureDlgOcrSchemeCaption": "Schematic (not actual UI)",
  "captureActiveBehaviorNote": "Active behavior: after you drag-select or double-click to select text in another app (outside Formycareer), the app reads that selection after a short pause. Your clipboard may change; avoid Auto capture while you must keep clipboard contents. SelectionHost (UIA) and clipboard listening are not used.",
